#: src/renderer/src/components/help/UserManual.tsx
msgid "<0>Emergency off</0> at the right of the top bar sets all 512 channels to 0 at once, in Show and in Setup mode, with or without a project. The fixtures, presets and scenes stay as they are; the faders show 0."
msgstr "<0>Emergency off</0> at the right of the top bar sets all 512 channels to 0 at once, in Show and in Setup mode, with or without a project. The fixtures, presets and scenes stay as they are; the faders show 0."

#: src/renderer/src/components/fixtures/FixtureChannelHelp.tsx
msgid "<0>Values</0> sets where the fader stops. <1>Continuous</1> goes through every value from min to max, e.g. a dimmer that does nothing below 100. <2>Steps</2> goes from min to max by the step size, e.g. a strobe in steps of 10. <3>Positions</3> stops only at the values listed, each with an optional name, e.g. the slots of a gobo wheel at 5, 6 and 200: the fader shows a tick for each (its name on mouse over), and a preset picks one of them. With <4>Buttons</4> next to Add position, the Show view has a button per position instead of the fader, the highest value on top. Only the fixture's faders follow these, the Channels view sends any value."
msgstr "<0>Values</0> sets where the fader stops. <1>Continuous</1> goes through every value from min to max, e.g. a dimmer that does nothing below 100. <2>Steps</2> goes from min to max by the step size, e.g. a strobe in steps of 10. <3>Positions</3> stops only at the values listed, each with an optional name, e.g. the slots of a gobo wheel at 5, 6 and 200: the fader shows a tick for each (its name on mouse over), and a preset picks one of them. With <4>Buttons</4> next to Add position, the Show view has a button per position instead of the fader, the highest value on top. Only the fixture's faders follow these, the Channels view sends any value."

#: src/renderer/src/components/fixtures/FixturePresetHelp.tsx
msgid "A <0>preset</0> is a button on the fixture that sets several channels at once, e.g. \"Warm white\". The channels it leaves unticked stay as they are. To make one quickly, set the faders and press the save button next to the presets."
msgstr "A <0>preset</0> is a button on the fixture that sets several channels at once, e.g. \"Warm white\". The channels it leaves unticked stay as they are. To make one quickly, set the faders and press the save button next to the presets."

