msgstr "A channel's min can't be above its max"

#: src/renderer/src/i18n/messages/fixtureMessages.ts
msgid "A channel's step size must be a whole number from 1"
msgstr "A channel's step size must be a whole number from 1"

#: src/renderer/src/i18n/messages/fixtureMessages.ts
msgid "A color must be a hex value like #ff00ff"
msgstr "A color must be a hex value like #ff00ff"

#: src/renderer/src/components/help/UserManual.tsx
msgid "A fixture is one device of your rig, e.g. a PAR or a smoke machine. In Setup mode, press <0>Add fixture</0> in the <1>Show</1> view:"
msgstr "A fixture is one device of your rig, e.g. a PAR or a smoke machine. In Setup mode, press <0>Add fixture</0> in the <1>Show</1> view:"

#: src/renderer/src/components/help/UserManual.tsx
msgid "A fixture's channel can have a <0>Max while locked</0> (in the fixture editor): while the channel lock is on, the channel never goes above it, whichever fader, preset, scene or view sets it. A laser gets 0, a macro channel running the device's own programs e.g. 50. Its faders show a lock and stop at the maximum (at 0 they are greyed out), and a preset that would set it higher is disabled. A scene that would set it higher stays playable, so a look of the whole rig still works: the channel only goes up to its maximum, and the scene's button shows a lock."
msgstr "A fixture's channel can have a <0>Max while locked</0> (in the fixture editor): while the channel lock is on, the channel never goes above it, whichever fader, preset, scene or view sets it. A laser gets 0, a macro channel running the device's own programs e.g. 50. Its faders show a lock and stop at the maximum (at 0 they are greyed out), and a preset that would set it higher is disabled. A scene that would set it higher stays playable, so a look of the whole rig still works: the channel only goes up to its maximum, and the scene's button shows a lock."

#: src/renderer/src/i18n/messages/fixtureMessages.ts
msgid "A position name can have at most {maxLength} characters"
msgstr "A position name can have at most {maxLength} characters"

#: src/renderer/src/components/help/UserManual.tsx
msgid "A preset is a button on a fixture that sets several of its channels at once, e.g. \"Warm white\". To make one, set the fixture's faders and press the save button next to its presets. Edit the fixture to rename a preset, give it a color (a dot on its button) or choose which channels it sets: the ones it leaves out stay as they are."
msgstr "A preset is a button on a fixture that sets several of its channels at once, e.g. \"Warm white\". To make one, set the fixture's faders and press the save button next to its presets. Edit the fixture to rename a preset, give it a color (a dot on its button) or choose which channels it sets: the ones it leaves out stay as they are."

#: src/renderer/src/i18n/messages/fixtureMessages.ts
msgid "A preset name can have at most {maxLength} characters"
msgstr "A preset name can have at most {maxLength} characters"

#: src/renderer/src/components/project/ProjectStartView.tsx
msgid "A project is a .glp file with the fixtures and scenes of one rig, e.g. one per venue or show. Keep it wherever you like: in Documents, on the Desktop or on a USB stick. Every change is saved to the file right away. The app opens the last project again on its next start, and a double-click on a .glp file opens it."
msgstr "A project is a .glp file with the fixtures and scenes of one rig, e.g. one per venue or show. Keep it wherever you like: in Documents, on the Desktop or on a USB stick. Every change is saved to the file right away. The app opens the last project again on its next start, and a double-click on a .glp file opens it."

#: src/renderer/src/components/help/UserManual.tsx
msgid "A scene is a button above the fixtures that sets the channels of several fixtures at once, e.g. \"Intro\" or \"Blackout\". The fixtures a scene leaves out stay as they are, so scenes can be layered: a colour scene for the PARs while the smoke machine keeps running."
msgstr "A scene is a button above the fixtures that sets the channels of several fixtures at once, e.g. \"Intro\" or \"Blackout\". The fixtures a scene leaves out stay as they are, so scenes can be layered: a colour scene for the PARs while the smoke machine keeps running."

#: src/renderer/src/i18n/messages/sceneMessages.ts
msgid "A scene name can have at most {maxLength} characters"
msgstr "A scene name can have at most {maxLength} characters"

#: src/renderer/src/components/help/UserManual.tsx
msgid "Add a <0>channel</0> for every entry of the device's channel list you want to control. Its <1>offset</1> is its number in the manual minus 1: channel 1 has offset 0, channel 2 offset 1."
msgstr "Add a <0>channel</0> for every entry of the device's channel list you want to control. Its <1>offset</1> is its number in the manual minus 1: channel 1 has offset 0, channel 2 offset 1."

#: src/renderer/src/components/fixtures/FixtureChannelHelp.tsx
msgid "Add a <0>channel</0> for every entry of the list you want to control, named as you like. Its <1>offset</1> is its number in the manual minus 1: channel 1 has offset 0, channel 2 offset 1, and so on. Leave out the ones you don't need, the gaps are fine."
msgstr "Add a <0>channel</0> for every entry of the list you want to control, named as you like. Its <1>offset</1> is its number in the manual minus 1: channel 1 has offset 0, channel 2 offset 1, and so on. Leave out the ones you don't need, the gaps are fine."

