#: src/renderer/src/components/help/UserManual.tsx
msgid "The app always starts in <0>Show mode</0>: the fixtures, their presets and the scenes can be played, but not changed, and the Channels view is off. Anything else needs <1>Setup mode</1>: in the <2>Settings</2> view, press <3>Unlock Setup mode</3> and type the password. The first time, there is no password yet: the one you type (twice) becomes it. The app then goes to the Show view; while Setup mode is open, the top bar says so."
msgstr "The app always starts in <0>Show mode</0>: the fixtures, their presets and the scenes can be played, but not changed, and the Channels view is off. Anything else needs <1>Setup mode</1>: in the <2>Settings</2> view, press <3>Unlock Setup mode</3> and type the password. The first time, there is no password yet: the one you type (twice) becomes it. The app then goes to the Show view; while Setup mode is open, the top bar says so."

#: src/renderer/src/components/help/UserManual.tsx
msgid "The app remembers the port it was last connected to, also after a Disconnect, and chooses it again on the next start. It always starts disconnected, so nothing is sent before you press Connect. Plugged the widget in after starting the app? Search the serial ports again in the Settings, then press Connect."
msgstr "The app remembers the port it was last connected to, also after a Disconnect, and chooses it again on the next start. It always starts disconnected, so nothing is sent before you press Connect. Plugged the widget in after starting the app? Search the serial ports again in the Settings, then press Connect."

#: src/renderer/src/components/help/DataFolderSection.tsx
msgid "The app's own settings are stored here as JSON files: the password hash, the output port, the language, the recent projects and the window position. The fixtures and scenes are in the project files."
msgstr "The app's own settings are stored here as JSON files: the password hash, the output port, the language, the recent projects and the window position. The fixtures and scenes are in the project files."

#: src/renderer/src/components/fixtures/FixtureChannelHelp.tsx
msgid "The arrows move a channel up or down: the fixture's faders are shown in the order of this list. Its offset and address stay as they are, and its presets and scenes keep setting it."
msgstr "The arrows move a channel up or down: the fixture's faders are shown in the order of this list. Its offset and address stay as they are, and its presets and scenes keep setting it."

#: src/renderer/src/components/help/UserManual.tsx
msgid "The channel lock is on after every start, independent of the mode. Lift it in the <0>Settings</0> view, e.g. for a show where the laser hangs high enough: in Show mode with the password, in Setup mode with a confirmation. It then stays lifted, also in Show mode and after Lock, until <1>Turn channel lock on</1> or a restart; the top bar shows <2>Channel lock lifted</2> meanwhile. Turned on again, the locked channels drop to their maximum right away."
msgstr "The channel lock is on after every start, independent of the mode. Lift it in the <0>Settings</0> view, e.g. for a show where the laser hangs high enough: in Show mode with the password, in Setup mode with a confirmation. It then stays lifted, also in Show mode and after Lock, until <1>Turn channel lock on</1> or a restart; the top bar shows <2>Channel lock lifted</2> meanwhile. Turned on again, the locked channels drop to their maximum right away."

